            <ArticleTitle>[Neuropathic pain, assessment and management].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>19-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In the case of neuropathic pain, clinical symptoms are not in proportion to the initial lesion. Its detection is based on the detailed description given by the patient, and on a meticulous clinical examination. Its treatment has many facets, from medication to multi-dimensional therapies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
